isplay": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1426, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1426, "cached_input": 31280, "input": 32708, "output": 153}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 38603, "other": 423, "system": 36063, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 8312}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 97798}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "56f23723-3972-5704-98c3-b3c80b7e1a2a", "at": 1795685735.370215, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84551, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "8b8cb0b4c74eb8810ab00c9b81dd4a78", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "7e737cd7-5908-527a-93a4-cf004605b8b9", "at": 1795685735.3727643, "until": 1795685737.3990614, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84552, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "8b8cb0b4c74eb8810ab00c9b81dd4a78", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01BuB7meBGeMG4zMWgJthETL", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "forge api repos/world/story-repo/wiki/page/Outline 2>&1 | python3 -c \" import sys,json,base64,re d=json.load(sys.stdin);t=base64.b64decode(d['content_base64']).decode() i=t.find('## Venue frame');print(t[i:i+1800])\"", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "forge api repos/world/story-repo/wiki/page/Outline 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json,base64,re\nd=json.load(sys.stdin);t=base64.b64decode(d['content_base64']).decode()\ni=t.find('## Venue frame');print(t[i:i+1800])\""]], "output": "```console\n## Venue frame (venue-repo, `story-repo`#4)\nNeurIPS 2026 Main Track; **9 content pages including figures and tables**; references, appendix and checklist outside. **Contribution type: General** (an evaluation paper: controlled comparison, bias–variance accounting, ceiling analysis), also if the headline turns out conditional or negative: \"Negative Results\" is not chosen (high significance/originality bar). **Main body: 7 items** — Fig. 1, Table 2, Fig. 2, Fig. 3, Fig. 4, Fig. 5, Fig. 6 (Fig. 1 is a small schematic). Everything else is appendix: Table 1 (audit and split/target counts), Table 3, Table 4, Fig. 5b, per-benchmark tables. Evidence a claim rests on is in the main body: the main text carries the k targets / #families per split in Table 2's columns and one sentence on thin cells, and says where Table 1 is. Writing profile: abstract one paragraph ≈ 130–260 words stating claims, scope and the headline; introduction ≈ 550–1500 words with the result stated; first figure on page 1–2; short related work in the main text, long version in the appendix; the checklist's \"Claims\" item is checked against the evidence.\n\n## 0. The paper in one paragraph\nEvaluating an LLM on a full benchmark is costly, so we run it on n ≪ N items and predict its full score. Existing methods (anchor points, tinyBenchmarks, metabench, assessor, active acquisition) use the score matrix of *source models* to pick items and fit a *latent model* of the target; they are judged mostly on held-out models that resemble the sources. We cast the problem as **finite-population estimation of a mean of N unknown 0/1 values with a free covariate (the source matrix)**. That frame separates what the sources can buy — **variance reduction** — from what must be controlled by design — **bias**. We (i) test, on 13\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "cb2c0e21-477e-5c08-9375-b46c3dd90f0f", "at": 179568